qemu_plugin: build hotloops out-of-tree

Relocate the hotloops hot-inner-loop detector out of the QEMU source tree
(it used to live in contrib/plugins/) into the repo's existing out-of-tree
plugin build under qemu_plugin/, so plugin sources are never committed into
QEMU.

- qemu_plugin/hotloops.c: the TCG plugin. G_GNUC_UNUSED on the unused
  callback params so it builds clean under the Makefile's -Wextra.
- qemu_plugin/Makefile: also build libhotloops.so; the shared
  qemu-plugin.h check is now an order-only prerequisite (DRY).
- scripts/hotloops.sh: the wrapper, repointed at the out-of-tree layout
  (build/qemu/qemu-system-*, qemu_plugin/libhotloops.so).
- docs/hotloops.md.

Build: make -C qemu_plugin QEMU_ROOT=$PWD/QEMU

